[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3217918972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109918#issuecomment-3217918972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109918","id":3217918972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_zYv8","user":{"login":"the-bham","id":7716848,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTY4NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7716848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham","html_url":"https://github.com/the-bham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-bham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T07:52:04Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T07:53:45Z","body":"hmm investigating further this is only an \"issue\" in editor releases which are installed by default by all package managers, official releases, godotenv as the symlink for the godot app.  the editor binary always defines TOOLS_ENABLED and thus if the packaged .pck/zip are used anywhere than a engine or project root (with precompiled .godot temp assemblies dir) it will fail to load .net assemblies.\n\nso if a developer wants to run a .net packaged godot game in headless or server environments (runs from command line) then either the engine needs to know its running from the command line and to look in project data directory,  or to use the template_release.exe of their specifi